#subtitle: Outside of electoral politics, the SPD runs a social world onto itself.
frequency: 250

= Party Organizations

In addition to being a political party, the SPD is a social world onto itself, with a vast array of associated organizations which serve the social needs of their members from cradle to grave.

Jungsozialisten (Jusos – Young Socialists) strength: [+ jung_strength +]

Sozialistische Arbeiter-Jugend (SAJ – Socialist Workers' Youth) strength: [+ saj_strength +]

[? if spd_world == 0: Currently, we are in the status of self segregation from bourgeouis society, filled with individualism, competitionship, nationalism, conservatism and even chauvinism. Our values form counter-culture against the mainstream of Weimar. ?] [? if spd_world == 1: We have demontaged the self segregation policy, starting the co-operation with bourgeouis society with ambivalent goals. Class struggle left argues against opening us, while reformists suggest that we could expose them to our socialist values, especially in proletariat dominated cultural organizations. ?]

[? if youth_crisis_spd >= 1: As the aging party, our youth organizations, comparably, are far smaller than our traditional groups. This was caused by the hyperinflationary crisis, from which both us and other traditional (primarily liberal) parties have not recovered from ever since. If we wish to attract them, naturally, we have to fund youth organizations and find the means to expand **beyond aging working class**, which means breaking through our rigid marxist thinking... ?]

- @newspapers: Fund more newspapers and journalists.
- @welfare: Fund more mutual aid and welfare programs.
- @culture: Fund sports leagues, educational, and cultural programs.
- @youth: We have the reputation of being a party for old men. Support the youth organizations.
- @spd_world_1: German Athletic Club invites us to co-operate with them. This will also open our own sub-world to the rest of Germany.
- @nothing: Do not increase funding for any program.
- @easy_discard

@spd_world_1
subtitle: Are we sure about that?
view-if: spd_world == 0
choose-if: resources >= 3 and reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength >= 60 and socialism < pro_republic and ideology != "Left" and ideology != "Centrist" and (peoples_party or new_middle_consciousness = 1)
unavailable-subtitle: [? if resources < 3: Not enough resources. ?] [? if reformist_strength + neorevisionist_strength < 60: Currently, this idea has no sufficient enough of support to consider doing this. ?] [? if ideology == Left or ideology == "Centrist": As the primarily marxist party, this can't possibly happen. ?] [? if not peoples_party or new_middle_consciousness = 1: We must expand our broad outlook on electorate. ?] [? if socialism >= pro_republic: With socialism trending, we can't possibly spend our efforts on working with unpopular bourgeouis. ?]
on-arrival: spd_world = 1; nationalism += 5 if nationalism > socialism; socialism += 5 if socialism > nationalism; pro_republic += 5; workers_spd += 5; workers += 1; neorevisionist_strength += 5; ddp_relation += 3; z_relation += 3; dvp_relation += 3; dnvp_relation += 2; rural_spd += 5 if peoples_party; old_middle_spd += 5 if peoples_party; new_middle_spd += 8 if peoples_party or new_middle_consciousness; socialism += 5; workers_dnvp += 3 if peoples_party; workers_dvp += 3 if peoples_party; workers_ddp += 3 if peoples_party

Our Workers’ Sports Federation has accepted German Athletic Club's proposal to co-operate after countless attempts of to do so. For the better or worse, the rest will follow the suit and unite the Germany's cultural world.

@newspapers
subtitle: Doubles party organizations timer.
on-arrival: media_timer = 0; party_organizations_timer = 16
go-to: media

# TODO: differing outcomes based on whether you've seen media, and what kind of media you've supported.


@welfare
choose-if: resources > 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
subtitle: -2 resources. [? if not black_thursday_seen: Currently, our members consider this as worthless spending. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; workers_aid += 1; unemployed_spd += 2*(1 - dissent); unemployed_spd += 2+(unemployed / 6) + (workers_aid / 2) if unemployed > 10 and workers_aid > 0

We have increased funding to Workers' Welfare. [? if black_thursday_seen > 0 : In an age of economic crisis, this will be helpful for improving our standing among the unemployed. ?]

@culture
choose-if: resources > 0
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
subtitle: -1 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 1; cultural_organizations += 1; left_dissent -= 6; center_dissent -= 6; labor_dissent -= 6; reformist_dissent -= 6; neorevisionist_dissent -= 6; z_relation -= 2 if historical_mode; ddp_relation -= 1 if historical_mode

It is not enough for the SPD to solely be a political party. The Worker Singer's League, Worker's Sports, and our schools and libraries are crucial to our members' lives. Funding these organizations makes our members more committed to the party, even when our policies might not be to their liking.

[? if sa_strength > 500 : However, it feels frivolous to spend on sports and choirs when the fascists are murdering us in the streets. ?]

@youth
choose-if: resources > 0
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
subtitle: -1 resources
on-arrival: resources -= 1; rb_strength += 50; rb_militancy += 0.02; jung_side = left_strength + neorevisionist_strength; jung_side += socialpatriot_strength if social_patriotism; jung_side += ethical_strength if ethical_socialism; saj_side = reformist_strength + center_strength

We are drawing in a new generation of members, and many of them also join the Reichsbanner, bringing fresh energy and militancy to its ranks.

However, our two youth organizations are clashing. The wing with the stronger backing in the party will decide which one gets our funds.

- @saj: Sozialistische Arbeiter-Jugend (SAJ – Socialist Workers' Youth) - our main youth organization.
- @jung: Jungsozialisten (Jusos – Young Socialists) - our young adult organization.

@jung
subtitle: This organization is filled with neorevisionists and leftists, who often clash with centrists and reformists.
choose-if: jung_side > saj_side
unavailable-subtitle: Our reformists and centrists hold more sway over the youth question. The Jusos will not get our funding.
on-arrival: jung_strength += 10; left_strength += 5; neorevisionist_strength += 5; socialpatriot_strength += 5 if social_patriotism; ethical_strength += 5 if ethical_socialism; radicalization += 1; young_socialists += 1; left_dissent -= 3; neorevisionist_dissent -= 3; socialpatriot_dissent -= 3 if social_patriotism; ethical_dissent -= 3 if ethical_socialism; center_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 2

We have funded the Young Socialists. Their ranks swell with radicals, neorevisionists [? if social_patriotism: , the Hamburg circle ?] [? if ethical_socialism: and ethical socialists ?], who push the party in a more militant direction. Centrists, reformists and laborites are unhappy about the new militancy.

@saj
subtitle: Our main organization, less political than Young Socialists.
choose-if: saj_side >= jung_side
unavailable-subtitle: Our left and neorevisionist currents hold more sway over the youth question. The SAJ will not get our funding.
on-arrival: saj_strength += 10; reformist_strength += 5; center_strength += 5; reformist_dissent -= 3; center_dissent -= 3; left_dissent += 3; neorevisionist_dissent += 3; socialpatriot_dissent += 3 if social_patriotism; ethical_dissent += 3 if ethical_socialism

We have funded the SAJ. Its members are loyal to the party leadership and fill our ranks with disciplined, moderate cadres. Leftists and neorevisionists [? if social_patriotism: , the Hamburg circle ?] [? if ethical_socialism: and ethical socialists ?] complain that the youth are being tamed.

@nothing

We do not fund any party organizations.

- @return: Continue...
